@EmployeeAPI_HostAddress = http://localhost:8080

### 1. Login (obtiene el token usado en todas las llamadas siguientes)
# @name login
POST {{EmployeeAPI_HostAddress}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "admin",
  "password": "admin"
}

@token = {{login.response.body.$.token}}

### 2. Health check (no requiere token)
GET {{EmployeeAPI_HostAddress}}/health

### 3. Crear un dispositivo
# @name createDevice
POST {{EmployeeAPI_HostAddress}}/api/device
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "name": "Reloj Recepcion",
  "location": "Casa Matriz",
  "timezone": "America/Santiago"
}

### 4. Crear un empleado (crea Departamento/Posición implícitamente si no existen)
# @name createEmployee
POST {{EmployeeAPI_HostAddress}}/api/employee
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "name": "Ana Perez",
  "email": "ana.perez@example.com",
  "dni": "12345678-9",
  "department": "Operaciones",
  "position": "Analista"
}

### 5. Enrolar al empleado con un PIN en el dispositivo
POST {{EmployeeAPI_HostAddress}}/api/enrollment
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "employee_Id": "{{createEmployee.response.body.$.id}}",
  "device_Id": "{{createDevice.response.body.$.id}}",
  "pin": "1111"
}

### 6. Registrar una marcación usando el PIN (simula lo que enviaría el reloj)
POST {{EmployeeAPI_HostAddress}}/api/punch
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "device_Id": "{{createDevice.response.body.$.id}}",
  "punchType": "IN",
  "pin": "1111"
}

### 7. Consultar empleados filtrados por departamento
GET {{EmployeeAPI_HostAddress}}/api/employee?departmentName=Operaciones
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 8. Consultar las marcaciones del empleado
GET {{EmployeeAPI_HostAddress}}/api/punch?employeeId={{createEmployee.response.body.$.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 9. Caso de error esperado: email duplicado -> debe devolver 409
POST {{EmployeeAPI_HostAddress}}/api/employee
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "name": "Otro Nombre",
  "email": "ana.perez@example.com",
  "department": "Operaciones",
  "position": "Analista"
}

### 10. Caso de error esperado: sin token -> debe devolver 401
GET {{EmployeeAPI_HostAddress}}/api/employee